      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the base 7 numbers \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) to base 10.\n2. Multiply the base 10 equivalents.\n3. Convert the product back to base 7.\n4. Find the sum of the digits of the base 7 product.\n\nLet's start with the conversion of the base 7 numbers to base 10.\n\nFirst, convert \\(24_7\\) to base 10:\n\\[24_7 = 2 \\cdot 7^1 + 4 \\cdot 7^0 = 2 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot 1 = 14 + 4 = 18_{10}\\]\n\nNext, convert \\(30_7\\) to base 10:\n\\[30_7 = 3 \\cdot 7^1 + 0 \\cdot 7^0 = 3 \\cdot 7 + 0 \\cdot 1 = 21 + 0 = 21_{10}\\]\n\nNow, multiply the base 10 equivalents:\n\\[18_{10} \\times 21_{10} = 378_{10}\\]\n\nNext, we need to convert \\(378_{10}\\) back to base 7. To do this, we repeatedly divide the number by 7 and keep track of the remainders.\n\n\\[378 \\div 7 = 54 \\text{ remainder } 0\\]\n\\[54 \\div 7 = 7 \\text{ remainder } 5\\]\n\\[7 \\div 7 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 0\\]\n\\[1 \\div 7 = 0 \\text{ remainder } 1\\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get \\(378_{10} = 1050_7\\).\n\nNow, we find the sum of the digits of \\(1050_7\\):\n\\[1 + 0 + 5 + 0 = 6\\]\n\nTherefore, the base seven sum of the digits of the product is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
