      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we first need to convert the base seven numbers \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) to base ten. Then, we will multiply these base ten numbers, convert the product back to base seven, and finally find the sum of the digits of the resulting base seven number.\n\nFirst, convert \\(24_7\\) to base ten:\n\\[\n24_7 = 2 \\cdot 7^1 + 4 \\cdot 7^0 = 2 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot 1 = 14 + 4 = 18\n\\]\nNext, convert \\(30_7\\) to base ten:\n\\[\n30_7 = 3 \\cdot 7^1 + 0 \\cdot 7^0 = 3 \\cdot 7 + 0 \\cdot 1 = 21\n\\]\nNow, multiply the base ten equivalents:\n\\[\n18 \\times 21 = 378\n\\]\nNext, we need to convert \\(378\\) from base ten to base seven. We do this by finding the largest power of 7 that fits into 378 and then proceeding with the remaining value:\n\\[\n7^3 = 343 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 7^4 = 2401\n\\]\nSince \\(343 \\leq 378 < 2401\\), the largest power of 7 that fits into 378 is \\(7^3 = 343\\). We divide 378 by 343 to get the coefficient for \\(7^3\\):\n\\[\n378 \\div 343 = 1 \\quad \\text{(quotient)} \\quad \\text{with a remainder of} \\quad 378 - 343 = 35\n\\]\nNext, we divide the remainder 35 by \\(7^2 = 49\\):\n\\[\n35 \\div 49 = 0 \\quad \\text{(quotient)} \\quad \\text{with a remainder of} \\quad 35\n\\]\nFinally, we divide the remainder 35 by \\(7^1 = 7\\):\n\\[\n35 \\div 7 = 5 \\quad \\text{(quotient)} \\quad \\text{with no remainder}\n\\]\nSo, the base seven representation of 378 is obtained by combining these coefficients: \\(150_7\\).\n\nNow, we need to find the sum of the digits of the base seven number \\(150_7\\):\n\\[\n1 + 5 + 0 = 6\n\\]\nTherefore, the base seven sum of the digits of the product is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
