      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to first convert the base seven numbers \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) to base ten, multiply them, and then convert the result back to base seven. Finally, we will find the base seven sum of the digits of the product.\n\nFirst, let's convert \\(24_7\\) to base ten. The base seven number \\(24_7\\) can be written as:\n\\[2 \\cdot 7^1 + 4 \\cdot 7^0 = 2 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot 1 = 14 + 4 = 18_{10}\\]\n\nNext, let's convert \\(30_7\\) to base ten. The base seven number \\(30_7\\) can be written as:\n\\[3 \\cdot 7^1 + 0 \\cdot 7^0 = 3 \\cdot 7 + 0 \\cdot 1 = 21 + 0 = 21_{10}\\]\n\nNow, we multiply the two base ten numbers:\n\\[18 \\cdot 21 = 378\\]\n\nNext, we need to convert \\(378_{10}\\) back to base seven. We do this by finding the highest powers of 7 that fit into 378 and then proceeding from there:\n\\[378 \\div 7^3 = 378 \\div 343 = 1 \\quad \\text{(remainder 345)}\\]\n\\[345 \\div 7^2 = 345 \\div 49 = 7 \\quad \\text{(remainder 1, which is 1 \\cdot 7^1)}\\]\n\\[1 \\div 7^1 = 1 \\div 7 = 0 \\quad \\text{(remainder 1, which is 1 \\cdot 7^0)}\\]\nSo, \\(378_{10} = 1 \\cdot 7^3 + 7 \\cdot 7^2 + 1 \\cdot 7^1 + 1 \\cdot 7^0 = 1711_7\\).\n\nNow, we need to find the sum of the digits of \\(1711_7\\):\n\\[1 + 7 + 1 + 1 = 10\\]\n\nTherefore, the base seven sum of the digits of the product is:\n\\[\\boxed{10}\\]",
